{"data": [{"author_id": "4398626122", "created_at": "2026-10-29T19:59:31.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115896329645723836"], "id": "2115896329645723836", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 239, "impression_count": 128034, "like_count": 1362, "quote_count": 82, "reply_count": 238, "retweet_count": 81}, "text": "Today, we’re sharing a look at our expanded system for monitoring frontier models at OpenAI, which in September helped us catch a model’s attempt to access the live internet during training.\n\nSince the Hugging Face incident—when models broke out of an internal cybersecurity", "url": "https://x.com/OpenAI/status/2115896329645723836"}, {"author_id": "1529761561170124800", "created_at": "2026-10-29T19:56:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115895634385649694"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/1lREBMcSUf", "end": 298, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/EpochAIResearch/status/2115895634385649694/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115895631197949952", "start": 275, "url": "https://t.co/1lREBMcSUf"}]}, "id": "2115895634385649694", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 10, "impression_count": 2911, "like_count": 45, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "The computing power of AI chips sold each quarter has grown 2.5× per year since the start of 2024. That’s down from roughly 6× in 2023, led by Nvidia’s then-new H100 GPU.\n\nSome evidence suggests growth slowed further. But quarterly sales are noisy, and our data ends just as https://t.co/1lREBMcSUf", "url": "https://x.com/EpochAIResearch/status/2115895634385649694"}, {"author_id": "1745106082790318080", "created_at": "2026-10-29T19:20:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115886444816298264"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/C4GoeQJFng", "end": 304, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2115886444816298264/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115886436473868288", "start": 281, "url": "https://t.co/C4GoeQJFng"}]}, "id": "2115886444816298264", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 9024, "like_count": 13, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "ClassOne Solstice Max at SEMICON West\n\nClassOne showcased its Solstice Max at SEMICON West. The 200/300mm single-wafer platform integrates electroplating, wet etch, strip and cleaning, and scales from 4 to 16 chambers. It targets advanced packaging metallization.\n\nSource: SEMICON https://t.co/C4GoeQJFng", "url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2115886444816298264"}, {"author_id": "2939913921", "created_at": "2026-10-29T18:58:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115881074115084733"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/archiehall/sta…", "end": 168, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/archiehall/status/2115851542511161620", "start": 145, "url": "https://t.co/yyIbiEtHFH"}]}, "id": "2115881074115084733", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 5, "impression_count": 3413, "like_count": 32, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 12, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115851542511161620", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Glad to see more institutions exploring the ideas here. I don’t think it’s cut and dry that distillation is bad for the US’s AI competitiveness. https://t.co/yyIbiEtHFH", "url": "https://x.com/natolambert/status/2115881074115084733"}, {"author_id": "1353836358901501952", "created_at": "2026-10-29T18:22:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115871889549865429"], "id": "2115871889549865429", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 452, "impression_count": 190337, "like_count": 1695, "quote_count": 141, "reply_count": 481, "retweet_count": 117}, "text": "We’ve trained Claude to flag potential misuse in conversations, a technique we call self-assessment. Right after it responds, Claude gives a preliminary safety assessment of the conversation. \n\nSince we began using self-assessment in June, it has surfaced misuse that our other", "url": "https://x.com/AnthropicAI/status/2115871889549865429"}, {"author_id": "2465283662", "created_at": "2026-10-29T16:32:27.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115844222729507001"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Join the discussion on this paper page", "display_url": "huggingface.co/papers/2610.29…", "end": 103, "expanded_url": "https://huggingface.co/papers/2610.29702", "images": [{"height": 648, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115844224520450048/pu1x0jN-?format=png&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115844224520450048/pu1x0jN-?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 80, "status": 200, "title": "Paper page - CausGround: Causal Interaction Grounding for Adaptive Embodied Planning", "unwound_url": "https://huggingface.co/papers/2610.29702", "url": "https://t.co/Fbd9VRf60Z"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/a1N8UqLlHk", "end": 127, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/_akhaliq/status/2115844222729507001/video/1", "media_key": "13_2115844150599802881", "start": 104, "url": "https://t.co/a1N8UqLlHk"}]}, "id": "2115844222729507001", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 4, "impression_count": 4888, "like_count": 13, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 2}, "text": "CausGround\n\nCausal Interaction Grounding for Adaptive Embodied Planning\n\npaper: https://t.co/Fbd9VRf60Z https://t.co/a1N8UqLlHk", "url": "https://x.com/_akhaliq/status/2115844222729507001"}, {"author_id": "2465283662", "created_at": "2026-10-29T16:29:23.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115843451078217750"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Join the discussion on this paper page", "display_url": "huggingface.co/papers/2610.20…", "end": 91, "expanded_url": "https://huggingface.co/papers/2610.20832", "images": [{"height": 648, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115843453062139909/egL6Brbz?format=png&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115843453062139909/egL6Brbz?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 68, "status": 200, "title": "Paper page - Amortizing Sequential Experimental Design in Reasoning LLMs", "unwound_url": "https://huggingface.co/papers/2610.20832", "url": "https://t.co/3EaEmuvJOn"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/Emj50LSkpQ", "end": 115, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/_akhaliq/status/2115843451078217750/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115843415220912128", "start": 92, "url": "https://t.co/Emj50LSkpQ"}]}, "id": "2115843451078217750", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 7, "impression_count": 4990, "like_count": 16, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 4, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "Amortizing Sequential Experimental Design in Reasoning LLMs\n\npaper: https://t.co/3EaEmuvJOn https://t.co/Emj50LSkpQ", "url": "https://x.com/_akhaliq/status/2115843451078217750"}, {"author_id": "2465283662", "created_at": "2026-10-29T16:25:15.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115842408302924162"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Join the discussion on this paper page", "display_url": "huggingface.co/papers/2610.32…", "end": 121, "expanded_url": "https://huggingface.co/papers/2610.32749", "images": [{"height": 648, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115646829979414528/mOdnEyw7?format=png&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115646829979414528/mOdnEyw7?format=png&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 98, "status": 200, "title": "Paper page - Efficient Streaming Audio-Visual Target Speaker Extraction for Real-World Acoustic Scenes", "unwound_url": "https://huggingface.co/papers/2610.32749", "url": "https://t.co/mDd8CAXlcr"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/atsggSbOez", "end": 145, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/_akhaliq/status/2115842408302924162/video/1", "media_key": "13_2115842310327992320", "start": 122, "url": "https://t.co/atsggSbOez"}]}, "id": "2115842408302924162", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 8, "impression_count": 4637, "like_count": 12, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 2, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "Efficient Streaming Audio-Visual Target Speaker Extraction for Real-World Acoustic Scenes\n\npaper: https://t.co/mDd8CAXlcr https://t.co/atsggSbOez", "url": "https://x.com/_akhaliq/status/2115842408302924162"}, {"author_id": "2939913921", "created_at": "2026-10-29T16:17:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115840347087814713"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/sytaylor/statu…", "end": 282, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/sytaylor/status/2115747212852363548", "start": 259, "url": "https://t.co/4xwhFGtVLA"}]}, "id": "2115840347087814713", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 90, "impression_count": 14060, "like_count": 259, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 39, "retweet_count": 11}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115747212852363548", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "This is very needed. Talking to models like Claude about anything that has an overlap with an area like legal, healthcare, etc is mind numbing. They’re so desperate to hedge and steer away from grey area that they often are really avoiding the real question. https://t.co/4xwhFGtVLA", "url": "https://x.com/natolambert/status/2115840347087814713"}, {"author_id": "778764142412984320", "created_at": "2026-10-29T15:30:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115828507712327979"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 27, "id": "1667249535519805451", "start": 17, "username": "MistralAI"}], "urls": [{"description": "The Science Behind the Open Cyber Frontier with Mistral Large 4Be...", "display_url": "youtu.be/FczbSauVvjw", "end": 262, "expanded_url": "https://youtu.be/FczbSauVvjw", "images": [{"height": 720, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115828554961129472/21kjqqQb?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1280}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115828554961129472/21kjqqQb?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 239, "status": 200, "title": "Science Behind the Open Cyber Frontier with Mistral Large 4", "unwound_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FczbSauVvjw&feature=youtu.be", "url": "https://t.co/JOyEpqGBO9"}]}, "id": "2115828507712327979", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 35, "impression_count": 24347, "like_count": 155, "quote_count": 5, "reply_count": 43, "retweet_count": 26}, "text": "We sat down with @MistralAI's Pierre Stock and Sagar Vaze from Mistral on launch day of Mistral Large 4. \n\nOpen weights. Trained in Mistral’s own data centers. Excels at cyber.\n\nFull conversation on cyber, training, evals and sandboxing:\n\nhttps://t.co/JOyEpqGBO9", "url": "https://x.com/huggingface/status/2115828507712327979"}, {"author_id": "2465283662", "created_at": "2026-10-29T15:21:11.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115826286652248275"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "Join the discussion on this paper page", "display_url": "huggingface.co/papers/2610.35…", "end": 120, "expanded_url": "https://huggingface.co/papers/2610.35684", "images": [{"height": 648, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115727676304756736/IxPNbTBG?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115727676304756736/IxPNbTBG?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 97, "status": 200, "title": "Paper page - OmniShowcase: Omnidirectional Subject-Consistent Video Generation from Multi-View Images", "unwound_url": "https://huggingface.co/papers/2610.35684", "url": "https://t.co/wcU8KWIRB5"}, {"display_url": "pic.x.com/t6zhZGTVMV", "end": 144, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/_akhaliq/status/2115826286652248275/video/1", "media_key": "13_2115826137192374272", "start": 121, "url": "https://t.co/t6zhZGTVMV"}]}, "id": "2115826286652248275", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 25, "impression_count": 6943, "like_count": 41, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 7}, "text": "OmniShowcase\n\nOmnidirectional Subject-Consistent Video Generation from Multi-View Images\n\npaper: https://t.co/wcU8KWIRB5 https://t.co/t6zhZGTVMV", "url": "https://x.com/_akhaliq/status/2115826286652248275"}, {"author_id": "1353836358901501952", "created_at": "2026-10-29T15:18:40.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115825653539025142"], "entities": {"urls": [{"description": "We’re highlighting 20 scientific foundations, institutions, and research groups from around the world that we’ve partnered with in an expansion of our AI for Science program.", "display_url": "anthropic.com/news/ai-for-sc…", "end": 187, "expanded_url": "https://www.anthropic.com/news/ai-for-science-expands-foundations-research-institutions", "images": [{"height": 630, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115541995137466368/0daYuU3Q?format=jpg&name=orig", "width": 1200}, {"height": 150, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/news_img/2115541995137466368/0daYuU3Q?format=jpg&name=150x150", "width": 150}], "start": 164, "status": 200, "title": "AI for Science expands to foundations and institutions", "unwound_url": "https://www.anthropic.com/news/ai-for-science-expands-foundations-research-institutions", "url": "https://t.co/oTu04tU4Pk"}]}, "id": "2115825653539025142", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 339, "impression_count": 195691, "like_count": 2519, "quote_count": 95, "reply_count": 304, "retweet_count": 189}, "text": "We’ve expanded our AI for Science program beyond individual teams to support some of the world’s leading scientific foundations, institutions, and research groups. https://t.co/oTu04tU4Pk", "url": "https://x.com/AnthropicAI/status/2115825653539025142"}, {"author_id": "12497", "created_at": "2026-10-29T15:02:50.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115821668350435645"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "x.com/jsnnsa/status/…", "end": 191, "expanded_url": "https://twitter.com/jsnnsa/status/2115623382721126826", "start": 168, "url": "https://t.co/yIqxMQRpqt"}]}, "id": "2115821668350435645", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1398, "impression_count": 92260, "like_count": 930, "quote_count": 8, "reply_count": 129, "retweet_count": 45}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2115623382721126826", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Fascinating case study of the sharpest edge of what you can do with agentic engineering in the Fable era - my eyebrows raised at least a dozen times while reading this https://t.co/yIqxMQRpqt", "url": "https://x.com/simonw/status/2115821668350435645"}, {"author_id": "1745106082790318080", "created_at": "2026-10-29T15:01:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115821309137465536"], "entities": {"mentions": [{"end": 32, "id": "1923440305703092226", "start": 20, "username": "sgl_project"}], "urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/tNM38ZR5E3", "end": 302, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2115821309137465536/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115821306780262401", "start": 279, "url": "https://t.co/tNM38ZR5E3"}]}, "id": "2115821309137465536", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 55, "impression_count": 24099, "like_count": 209, "quote_count": 7, "reply_count": 27, "retweet_count": 17}, "text": "ALERT🚨: GB300 NVL72 @sgl_project can get close to 1000 tok/s/user on DeepSeek Flash v4.1 by aggressively fusing kernels together!!\n\nTileRT started this trend in the ecosystem of megakernel engines on OSS frontier models! Glad to see SGLang widely adopting it!\n\nGreat work by the https://t.co/tNM38ZR5E3", "url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2115821309137465536"}, {"author_id": "1745106082790318080", "created_at": "2026-10-29T01:38:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2115619227381928400"], "entities": {"urls": [{"display_url": "pic.x.com/OYrSn5Yu5I", "end": 23, "expanded_url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2115619227381928400/photo/1", "media_key": "3_2115619224970240000", "start": 0, "url": "https://t.co/OYrSn5Yu5I"}]}, "id": "2115619227381928400", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 189, "impression_count": 129064, "like_count": 2965, "quote_count": 14, "reply_count": 32, "retweet_count": 86}, "text": "https://t.co/OYrSn5Yu5I", "url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2115619227381928400"}, {"author_id": "2465283662", "created_at": "2026-10-28T21:58:07.000Z",